/target/
/dist/
Cargo.lock

# CRA-3: pqc-sig-wasm/ and tests/downstream-consumer-fixture/ are separate
# Cargo packages (each its own [workspace] root, own target/), not just
# nested build output of the root crate -- the root-anchored /target above
# doesn't reach them.
pqc-sig-wasm/target
tests/downstream-consumer-fixture/target

# Both are artifact-shaped crates (like pqc-kem-wasm), not libraries -- their
# lock files ARE committed for reproducible CI builds (`cargo build --locked`
# in ci.yml), unlike the root Cargo.lock above, which follows the usual
# library-crate convention of leaving lockfile pinning to downstream
# consumers. The bare `Cargo.lock` pattern above would otherwise swallow
# these nested ones too.
!pqc-sig-wasm/Cargo.lock
!tests/downstream-consumer-fixture/Cargo.lock
